  "sources": [
    "https://help.evernote.com/hc/en-us/articles/34296687388307-Keyboard-shortcuts"
  ],
  "note": "Desktop app (Windows/Mac). \"Global\" context = system-wide hotkeys that fire whenever Evernote is running, even outside the app; all other contexts require Evernote to be focused. \"Select single\" (Cmd/Ctrl+Click) and \"Select group\" (Shift+Click) are mouse-modifier combos and not expressible; skipped. \"Top of note list\" and \"Bottom of note list\" now include the documented Mac Fn+Left/Fn+Right chords alongside the Windows Home/End bindings, since the chord grammar accepts Fn as a mac-only modifier. \"Focus on note list\" uses Cmd+| on Mac (the pipe character is not an expressible key) so only the Windows Alt+Ctrl+\\ binding is listed. \"Align left\" (Option+Cmd+{) and \"Align right\" (Option+Cmd+}) use curly-brace symbols not in the punctuation set, so only the Windows Ctrl+L / Ctrl+J bindings are listed. \"Increase font size\" (Shift+Cmd+>) and \"Decrease font size\" (Shift+Cmd+<) use angle-bracket symbols not in the punctuation set on both platforms, so both are skipped entirely. \"Hide Evernote\" and \"Quit Evernote\" have no Windows equivalent per the source. \"Add comment\" on Windows (Ctrl+Shift+M) only fires if text is already selected. The Auto formatting section (typed triggers like #, [+], '>', ':elephant:') types literal characters into the note as you type rather than firing a fixed shortcut, so it is not expressible and is skipped entirely.",
